Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.06,0:00:05.06,Header,,0,0,0,,This is a Gentlemen of the Hàn free fansub.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.58,0:00:05.82,Episode Title,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,750,4500,5300)\pos(640,454.382)}Episode 64\N\N\N\N\NPacifying the Five Forces
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.39,0:00:31.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, please accept my respects.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.38,0:00:34.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.82,0:00:39.98,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(290,478)}Liú Bèi\NStyled: Xuándé
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.48,0:00:40.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Liegemen, excused.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.31,0:00:45.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, Chancellor, sit on the bed.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.14,0:00:51.02,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(810,400)}Zhūgě Liàng\NStyled: Kǒngmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.23,0:01:02.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,660)}{\bord14}It was Chancellor's service...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.18,0:01:05.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,660)}{\bord14}...that let Us achieve Our imperial enterprise.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.41,0:01:11.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,660)}{\bord14}It was only through Our short-sightedness...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.22,0:01:18.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}...that We would lose so grievously, against the Chancellor's advice.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.43,0:01:26.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Now We are left with naught but grief and remorse, awaiting Our last breath.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.63,0:01:34.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,660)}{\bord14}The Crown Prince is feeble.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.29,0:01:42.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,660)}{\bord14}He cannot shoulder this great undertaking.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.82,0:00:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.62,0:01:49.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope that Your Majesty cares for your sacred body to fulfill the hopes of the realm.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.73,0:01:55.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, please care for your sacred body and recover soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.06,0:02:11.74,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(921,493)}Mǎ Sù\NStyled: Yòucháng
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.54,0:02:19.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Liegemen, stand down for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.66,0:02:21.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.31,0:02:33.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Chancellor, what are your thoughts on Ma Su?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.18,0:02:38.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}He is a great savant of our time.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.25,0:02:47.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}No, in Our view, his fame is an overstatement.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.50,0:02:50.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}He is not to be employed for greater duties.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.88,0:02:53.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Chancellor ought to consider this.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.97,0:02:57.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.41,0:03:07.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}This is Our penned edict.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.61,0:03:13.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Chancellor, please give it \Nto Crown Prince Liu Shan,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.85,0:03:18.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}and tell him not to treat this as ordinary words.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.29,0:03:24.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}We hope that you, Chancellor, will guide him with care.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.84,0:03:31.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.87,0:03:39.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}We are not well-educated, \NOur knowledge is only rough.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.27,0:03:42.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}The Great Sage once said:
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.08,0:03:46.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}"When a bird is about to die, its notes are mournful;
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.95,0:03:52.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}when a man is about to die, his words are good."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.62,0:03:52.78,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Analects{\i0} 8-4. Translation by James Legge.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.78,0:03:59.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}We wished to annihilate \Nthe Cao bandits with you all,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.66,0:04:06.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}and save the Imperial house of Han, but now We must depart midway.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.42,0:04:13.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope that Your Majesty rests your sacred body in repose.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.17,0:04:16.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I will bear the labor of dogs and horses,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.26,0:04:21.06,Default,,0,0,0,,in order to repay Your Majesty's kindness of patronage.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.70,0:04:23.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.21,0:04:25.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.32,0:04:31.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Before We die,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.98,0:04:37.34,Default,,0,0,0,,We have sincere words to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.30,0:04:40.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660.674)}Your Majesty, what sacred edict do you have?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.62,0:04:47.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660.674)}Your talents are ten times that of Cao Pi.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.35,0:04:55.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}You will certainly be able to secure and preserve the empire and attain Our great undertaking.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.70,0:05:00.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}If Crown Prince Liu Shan can be supported,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.05,0:05:02.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}then support him.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.42,0:05:06.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}If he is unworthy,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.70,0:05:14.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Chancellor, you may make yourself the master of Chengdu.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.47,0:05:23.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Your Majesty! How could I dare not to devote all my effort,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.91,0:05:27.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}even my life, to your noble house? I will serve loyally until my death!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.26,0:05:29.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.14,0:05:31.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.50,0:05:33.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Majesty!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.40,0:05:36.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, please rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.63,0:05:38.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Please rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.84,0:05:43.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.50,0:05:54.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Summon Liu Yong and Liu Li.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.25,0:06:01.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.48,0:06:06.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660.674)}Remember Our words well. After Our passing,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.90,0:06:09.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660.674)}you three brothers,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.14,0:06:13.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}must all serve the Chancellor with respect as if he were your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.43,0:06:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, father.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.42,0:06:18.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry and pay respects to Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.61,0:06:20.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Father-Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.79,0:06:24.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Please rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.37,0:06:26.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Please rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.06,0:06:30.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.39,0:06:35.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if I offered my life in sacrifice,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.55,0:06:38.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,700)}I could never repay Your Majesty's \Nkindness and patronage.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.34,0:06:40.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.82,0:06:46.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Summon the ministers.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.80,0:06:56.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.98,0:07:03.78,Default,,0,0,0,,We have entrusted our children to the Chancellor,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.81,0:07:09.42,Default,,0,0,0,,and ordered Crown Prince Liu Shan to treat him as if his own father.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.50,0:07:14.46,Default,,0,0,0,,You must not neglect this charge,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.59,0:07:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,and disappoint Us.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.77,0:07:20.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.53,0:07:23.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Zilong.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.50,0:07:26.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Zilong.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.74,0:07:32.62,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(967.411,504.27)}Zhào Yún\NStyled: Zǐlóng
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.71,0:07:29.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.70,0:07:38.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.63,0:07:47.98,Default,,0,0,0,,We and you, through all hardship,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.21,0:07:51.54,Default,,0,0,0,,remain bound together.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.33,0:07:58.90,Default,,0,0,0,,For the sake of our old bonds,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.82,0:08:04.86,Default,,0,0,0,,watch over my sons.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.10,0:08:08.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Do not let Us down.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.70,0:08:12.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I will serve them with all I have.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.54,0:08:23.78,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(329.333,478.667)}Liú Yǒng \NStyled: Gōngshòu
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.78,0:08:26.10,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(310.667,438.667)}Liú Lǐ\N Styled: Fèngxiào
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.10,0:08:28.46,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(250.,600)}Zhāng Bāo
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.46,0:08:30.83,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(299.2,454.4)}Guān Xīng\NStyled: Ānguó
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.34,0:08:34.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Sirs,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.01,0:08:40.42,Default,,0,0,0,,We cannot instruct each and every one of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.28,0:08:45.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Take care of yourselves...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.97,0:08:56.62,Default,,0,0,0,,-Your Majesty!\N-Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.13,0:09:06.50,Thinking,,0,0,0,,On the 24th day of the fourth month of \Nthe third year of Shu-Han's Zhangwu era, 223 CE,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.18,0:09:13.50,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Liu Bei passed away from illness at Baidi. He was sixty-three years old.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.51,0:09:52.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that Liu Bei is dead, We have no more worries.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.90,0:09:54.90,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(948.928,474.607)}Cáo Pī\NStyled: Zǐhuán
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.02,0:09:57.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Why not raise troops and attack while his land has no master?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.65,0:10:00.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, though Liu Bei is dead,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.66,0:10:04.86,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(965,490)}Jiá Xǔ\NStyled: Wénhé
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.42,0:10:02.70,Default,,0,0,0,,he entrusted his sons to Zhuge Liang,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.71,0:10:05.07,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,who, thankful for Liu Bei's kindness and favor,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.07,0:10:09.18,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,will certainly do his utmost to support Liu Shan, their young ruler.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.74,0:10:13.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, do not attack rashly.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.46,0:10:17.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, when else would be the time to attack if not now?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.02,0:10:17.26,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(305.,480)}Sīmǎ Yí\NStyled: Zhòngdá
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.02,0:10:21.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhongda's words match Our intent exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.69,0:10:25.34,Default,,0,0,0,,In your opinion, how should we advance?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.46,0:10:29.14,Default,,0,0,0,,With only the troops within our nation,\Nvictory will be very difficult.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.26,0:10:34.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Only a concerted attack using five forces\Nwith five hundred thousand troops in total,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.40,0:10:39.19,Default,,0,0,0,,can confuse Zhuge Liang and create an opportunity.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.06,0:10:42.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Where do these five forces come from?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.35,0:10:48.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhongda! How can there be five hundred \N thousand soldiers in the nation?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.10,0:10:50.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this not a jest?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.79,0:10:58.26,Default,,0,0,0,,In my view, five hundred thousand troops \Ncan be obtained easily.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.58,0:11:02.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhongda, what plans do you have for this?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.09,0:11:05.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,667.416)}Your Majesty can compose a letter,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.10,0:11:08.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}and send an envoy to the land of the Xianbei in Liaodong,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.34,0:11:10.18,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Xianbei (鮮卑) are semi-nomadic peoples of northern steppes, in modern day Mongolia and northeastern China.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.18,0:11:11.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,667.416)}to meet King Kebineng with gifts of gold and silk.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.01,0:11:15.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Have him raise one hundred thousand Qiang troops \Nfrom Liaoxi, to take Xiping Pass by land.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.98,0:11:15.08,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Qiāng(西羌): Northern nomadic peoples who lived\Nin Liang Province, northwest China.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.37,0:11:16.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}This is the first force.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.47,0:11:23.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Then, send an envoy with gifts and titles to Meng Huo, King of the South, in Nanzhong.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.51,0:11:26.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Order him to raise one hundred thousand \Ntroops to attack Yi Province
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.27,0:11:28.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}and its commanderies of Yongchang, Zangke, and Yuesui,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.35,0:11:30.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}striking the south of the Western Riverlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.90,0:11:32.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}This is the second force.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.73,0:11:34.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Then, send an envoy to improve\Nrelations with Eastern Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.83,0:11:37.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}With promises of land, order Sun Quan\Nto raise one hundred thousand troops,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.70,0:11:40.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}to attack the gorges of \Nthe Riverlands and Fucheng.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.40,0:11:41.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}This is the third force.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.39,0:11:45.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Then, one can send an envoy to\N Meng Da, the surrendered general,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.50,0:11:48.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}order him to lead one hundred\Nthousand troops in Shangyong,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.08,0:11:49.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}and attack westwards to Hanzhong.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.60,0:11:51.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}This is the fourth force.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.02,0:11:55.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Finally, appoint General Cao Zhen\Nas Grand Marshal,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.13,0:11:59.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}and order one hundred thousand troops to take\Nthe Riverlands from Jingzhao via Yangping Pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.45,0:12:01.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}This is the fifth force.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.27,0:12:05.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}These five armies, five hundred thousand\Nin strength, will advance together.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.86,0:12:12.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Even if Zhuge Liang had the talents \Nof Lü Wang, he could hardly stop them!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.98,0:12:12.02,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Lü Wang AKA Jiang Ziya, the leading strategist of Zhou who helped topple the Shang Dynasty. Formerly the main God of War in China.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.67,0:12:15.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Should this plan succeed,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.66,0:12:19.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}the force would be like a boulder crushing an egg. \NHow could Western Shu stop it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.26,0:12:22.74,Default,,0,0,0,,My liegemen.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.02,0:12:24.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.82,0:12:30.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Hear Our edict: Send the envoys and draft\Nthe letters. Attack Shu with all five forces!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.54,0:12:31.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.58,0:12:33.18,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(269,600)}Chengdu
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.90,0:12:35.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.02,0:12:38.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Pi has mobilized five armies\Nto attack the Western Riverlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.18,0:12:40.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, Your Majesty, make a decision at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.50,0:12:42.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Is the Chancellor aware?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.21,0:12:45.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I have reported this matter to the Chancellor,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.03,0:12:49.07,Default,,0,0,0,,but, for reasons unknown, the Chancellor is not leaving his residence.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.66,0:12:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,We are here to visit the Chancellor,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.14,0:12:57.80,Default,,0,0,0,,why aren't you letting us in?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.01,0:13:01.12,Default,,0,0,0,,The late Emperor entrusted\NHis Majesty to the Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.58,0:13:03.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, just as His Majesty ascends to the throne,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.75,0:13:08.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Pi has sent five forces to violate our\Nborders, and the situation is critical.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.30,0:13:11.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Why is the Chancellor feigning illness and staying in?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.77,0:13:13.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Sirs, sirs.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.81,0:13:15.62,Default,,0,0,0,,The Chancellor feels unwell.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.72,0:13:20.10,Default,,0,0,0,,You may discuss the matters tomorrow in the court.\NPlease return to your residences for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.34,0:13:22.45,Thinking,,0,0,0,,His Majesty has arrived!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.65,0:13:34.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.50,0:13:50.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.93,0:13:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is the Chancellor?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.34,0:13:53.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I do not know.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.49,0:13:58.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The Chancellor has ordered me to stop\Nall officials from entering.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.34,0:14:07.42,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(325,455)}Liú Shàn\NStyled: Gōngsì
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.31,0:14:25.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Does the Chancellor feel at ease?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.18,0:14:31.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I did not know of Your Majesty's arrival.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.22,0:14:33.61,Default,,0,0,0,,-My crime deserves death. \N-Father-Chancellor, please rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.74,0:14:39.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Cao Pi has sent five forces\Nto attack, we are nearing a crisis.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.51,0:14:43.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Father-Chancellor, why are you not coming out to attend to matters?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.22,0:14:48.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.81,0:14:49.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Father-Chancellor, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.22,0:14:57.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.17,0:15:04.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Your Majesty, the fact that Cao Pi's\Nfive forces are coming,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.83,0:15:07.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}how could I not know?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.87,0:15:10.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660.)}I was not watching fishes just now.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.51,0:15:12.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Instead, I was pondering.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.46,0:15:15.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Father-Chancellor, how\Nwill you repel the enemies?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.74,0:15:20.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Kebineng, the warlord, \NMeng Huo, the King of the South;
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.71,0:15:23.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Meng Da, the traitor general, \Nand Cao Zhen, the Wei general,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.54,0:15:27.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660.674)}all these four forces, I have already repelled!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.94,0:15:30.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660.674)}Oh!? Out of the five forces, four have been repelled?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.70,0:15:35.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Only the force of Sun Quan remains,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.30,0:15:37.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}though I do have a plan to repel it,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.78,0:15:42.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I need an eloquent man\Nto be an envoy to Eastern Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.83,0:15:47.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}As I could not find such a man, I was pondering.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.66,0:15:51.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Father-Chancellor, you do indeed\N have unfathomable designs!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.62,0:15:54.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}We would like to hear this plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.06,0:15:57.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}The late Emperor entrusted \NYour Majesty to my care,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.59,0:16:00.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I would not dare neglect\Nthat duty for an instant!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.09,0:16:04.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Even the best strategies are\Nundone if not kept secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.74,0:16:06.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}How could we share them\Nwith just anyone?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.86,0:16:21.25,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: This contradicts with Sima Yi's prior claim that Kebineng resides\N in Liaodong, which is to the northeast of the Three Kingdoms.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.86,0:16:21.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Vassal-King Kebineng threatens to attack Xiping Pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.21,0:16:26.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I know Ma Chao's clan has deep roots in the west, \Nand has the hearts of the Qiang living there.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.21,0:16:27.06,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Ma Chao's grandfather, Ma Ping (馬平) had lived among the Qiang.\NHis wife, Ma Chao's grandmother, was of Qiang descent.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.06,0:16:30.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}The Qiang respect Ma Chao as\Na great, nigh-heavenly general.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.04,0:16:33.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}I have sent an envoy to move day and night,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.77,0:16:36.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}to order Ma Chao to firmly defend Xiping Pass,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.85,0:16:39.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}and to lay four detachments\Nin ambush, rotating every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.70,0:16:44.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}With these troops in defense,\Nthis force is nothing to worry about!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.74,0:16:49.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Meng Huo, the King of the South, is\Ninvading the four commanderies.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.70,0:16:54.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I have sent Wei Yan to lead an army\N to move from the left to the right,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.55,0:16:58.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}and then move from the right\Nto the left, as misdirection.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.78,0:17:01.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}The Southern troops, brave but\Nknowing little of strategy,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.51,0:17:04.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}will certainly not advance.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.10,0:17:08.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}This force is nothing to worry about either!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.75,0:17:15.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Meng Da is leading a force towards Hanzhong.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.26,0:17:19.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Meng Da and Li Yan swore \Nto be friends to the death.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.23,0:17:24.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}When I was returning to Chengdu, \NI left Li Yan to guard Yong'an Palace.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.14,0:17:28.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I have written a letter in\NLi Yan's handwriting,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.41,0:17:30.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}and sent it to Meng Da.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.43,0:17:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Meng Da will feign illness\Nand decline to attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.65,0:17:36.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}This force is nothing to worry about either!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.11,0:17:41.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}How about Cao Zhen's force?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.77,0:17:45.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Cao Zhen is attacking Yangping Pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.01,0:17:49.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Its harsh terrain is easy to defend,\Nand difficult to conquer.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.03,0:17:54.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I have sent Zhao Yun with\Na detachment to defend it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.34,0:17:59.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}He only needs to fortify and stall,\Nand await the enemies' exhaustion.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.38,0:18:03.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Should Cao Zhen see our armies fortifying,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.46,0:18:06.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}he will withdraw of his own accord.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.00,0:18:14.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}In the snap of a finger, you have repelled\Nfour forces, Father-Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.08,0:18:18.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}None of these four forces warrant any worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.66,0:18:24.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}I feared for uncertainties,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.22,0:18:28.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}so I have secretly sent officers\NGuan Xing and Zhang Bao
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.54,0:18:32.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}to lead thirty thousand troops each\Nand garrison at critical places,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.66,0:18:35.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}so that they can support each detachment.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.14,0:18:41.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I made these arrangements\Nwithout going through Chengdu.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.66,0:18:44.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Therefore, nobody knows about them.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.50,0:18:48.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Regarding the forces of Sun Quan,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.22,0:18:52.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I have anticipated that it will not make rash movements.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.57,0:18:56.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}If the four forces were winning,\Nit would certainly attack;
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.33,0:18:58.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}should the four forces withdraw,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.67,0:19:02.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}how could it attack by itself?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.22,0:19:06.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}For this, I need an eloquent diplomat
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.86,0:19:10.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}to go to Eastern Wu, convince them with reason,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.07,0:19:12.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}and stop Sun Quan's advance.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.87,0:19:17.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}However, I have not found such a man. \NThus do I hesitate.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.11,0:19:22.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Forgive me for having troubled \NYour Majesty to make this visit.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.72,0:19:32.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.22,0:19:39.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Father-Chancellor, no need for escort.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.11,0:19:42.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, take care.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.50,0:20:02.54,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(989.855,481.348)}Dèng Zhī\NStyled: Bómiáo
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.16,0:20:03.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.90,0:20:06.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Five hundred thousand Wei troops\Nare coming. How do we repel them?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.90,0:20:08.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, how do we repel them?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.51,0:20:09.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.74,0:20:15.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.38,0:20:15.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.58,0:20:20.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Summon Deng Zhi.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.01,0:20:20.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.51,0:20:24.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Today, three nations stand against each other.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.37,0:20:26.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}If we were to strike at Wei and Wu,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.35,0:20:29.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}in your view, which should be attacked first?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.73,0:20:31.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}In my humble reasoning,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.66,0:20:34.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}though Wei is a traitor to\Nour Han Dynasty, its force is great.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.61,0:20:37.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}It cannot be shaken easily,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.02,0:20:41.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}so we must bide our time. His Majesty has just ascended to the throne;
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.82,0:20:44.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}with the people's confidence not yet\Nsteady, we should ally with Wu,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.95,0:20:48.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}promise mutual defense, and clear\Nthe late Emperor's old grievances.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.47,0:20:50.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}This is the plan for the long term.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.02,0:20:53.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660.)}I wonder what the Chancellor's opinions may be?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.98,0:20:57.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I have long wished to send\N an envoy to Eastern Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.75,0:21:00.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Sadly, I have not found the man.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.50,0:21:02.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660.)}Sir, since you understand this intent,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.32,0:21:06.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}you are the man to go to Eastern Wu!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.10,0:21:16.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Pi is raising four forces\Nto take the Western Riverlands,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.14,0:21:18.78,Default,,0,0,0,,and has asked Eastern Wu\Nto raise troops in support.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.98,0:21:22.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Any conquered land of the Western\NRiverlands will be split in half.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.26,0:21:28.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Boyan, what are your thoughts?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.46,0:21:33.86,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(970.052,453.034)}Lù Xùn\NStyled: Bóyán
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.46,0:21:31.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Pi sits in the Central Plains.\NHe should not be attacked now.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.98,0:21:35.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Rejection today will certainly\Ncreate an enemy tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.02,0:21:37.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness may agree for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.74,0:21:41.58,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(338,480)}Sūn Quán\NStyled: Zhòngmóu
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.10,0:21:39.69,Default,,0,0,0,,On one side, prepare our army.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.69,0:21:42.06,Default,,0,0,0,,On the other side, gather\N intel on the four forces.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.18,0:21:43.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Should the four forces win,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.67,0:21:47.57,Default,,0,0,0,,we send troops in support and take Chengdu first. \NThis is the superior strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.78,0:21:51.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Should the four forces be defeated,\Nthen we renegotiate.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.31,0:21:56.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.26,0:22:18.38,Default,,0,0,0,,When Deng Zhi comes, how\Nshould I answer him?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.98,0:22:23.78,Default,,0,0,0,,After killing Guan Yu and\Ndefeating Liu Bei,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.14,0:22:25.78,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(340,460)}Zhāng Zhāo\NStyled: Zǐbù
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.09,0:22:26.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Wu and Shu have incurred\Ndeep-seated resentment.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:27.06,0:22:29.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Cao Wei is showing\Nsigns of friendship with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.06,0:22:35.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, only allying with Wei\Nagainst Shu could bring peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.10,0:22:43.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, do not fall for Zhuge\NLiang's ploy of repulsing the forces,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.38,0:22:46.02,Default,,0,0,0,,and miss the excellent opportunity \Nof attacking Shu.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.26,0:22:50.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, offending Cao Wei\Nwould certainly incur ill consequences.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.33,0:22:57.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Summoning Deng Zhi,\Nthe envoy of Western Shu!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.14,0:23:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Greetings, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.14,0:23:32.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you not kneeling?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.90,0:23:37.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}The envoy of a greater state does not\Nprostrate before the lord of a lesser land.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.39,0:23:42.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Such arrogance!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.82,0:23:46.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Are you using that little tongue of yours,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.37,0:23:50.14,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,AKA Lì Yìjī (酈食其), an advisor of Liu Bang, Emperor Gaozu of Han,\Nduring the Chu-Han Contention. He was boiled alive by the King of Qi.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.37,0:23:50.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}to mimic Scholar Li persuading Qi?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.67,0:23:54.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}That cauldron in front of the hall is there for {\i1}you!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.72,0:23:57.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}They say that Eastern Wu\Nis manned by outstanding talent.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.94,0:24:02.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Who would have expected that\N the men in this court fear me, a mere scholar!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.17,0:24:07.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}How would I fear a baseborn like you?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.54,0:24:08.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}If you are not afraid of me,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.02,0:24:12.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}then why set up the cauldron and the soldiers?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.47,0:24:16.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}You are lobbying for Zhuge Liang,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.22,0:24:21.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}in order to turn me from Wei to Shu, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.14,0:24:24.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}I am but a scholar from the Riverlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:24.47,0:24:26.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660.674)}I am here for the interest of Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:26.65,0:24:30.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}However, Your Highness has set up soldiers and cauldrons to reject an envoy.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.66,0:24:33.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660.674)}A petty act of paltry men.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:41.01,0:24:42.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Dismissed.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:51.68,0:24:52.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Confer a seat.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.54,0:25:03.50,Default,,0,0,0,,What sort of interest does Wu have?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:04.66,0:25:06.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Please explain this, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:06.82,0:25:10.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, Cao Pi had sent\Nan envoy to come to Wu,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.98,0:25:13.74,Default,,0,0,0,,and invited Your Highness\Nto attack Shu together.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:13.90,0:25:15.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this the case?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:15.37,0:25:16.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:16.90,0:25:20.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Wishing to wait for the outcome,\NYour Highness has not raised the troops.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.64,0:25:21.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.46,0:25:27.31,Default,,0,0,0,,No. Due to provisions,\NI have not sent the troops.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:27.61,0:25:29.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Attacking would not bring victory,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.74,0:25:32.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}but not attacking would draw the ire of Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:32.51,0:25:36.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Then Your Highness would be at an impasse, unable to advance or withdraw.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.81,0:25:41.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Any slight miscalculation\Nwould bring great peril.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:42.07,0:25:45.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}How can it be said that\NEastern Wu is without worries?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:46.67,0:25:50.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Clearly it is the {\i1}Shu kingdom{\i0}\Nthat is in great peril.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:50.82,0:25:53.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Yet, you want us {\i1}Eastern Wu{\i0} to stand down?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:54.17,0:25:58.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}With an alliance of Wei, Wu, \Nand the five forces, Shu {\i1}will{\i0} fall.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:59.28,0:26:03.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Then, Wei and Wu shall\Nevenly divide the land of Shu!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:03.84,0:26:05.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Out of the five forces,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.09,0:26:08.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}four have been repelled by our Chancellor Zhuge!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:08.20,0:26:10.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Minister Zhang, are you aware of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:13.68,0:26:16.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, how frightening!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:16.46,0:26:17.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Report!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:19.22,0:26:20.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.64,0:26:21.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Speak.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:21.62,0:26:24.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Pi's four armies have all\Nwithdrawn without a fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:29.20,0:26:30.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Dismissed.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:30.16,0:26:30.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.42,0:26:45.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, Chancellor Zhuge is well-versed\Nin planning strategies and military affairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:45.54,0:26:48.34,Default,,0,0,0,,For this reason, he can fight\N against the enemy from afar.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:49.06,0:26:52.64,Default,,0,0,0,,The Qiang troops see Ma Chao \Nas a general with heavenly might.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:52.64,0:26:55.22,Default,,0,0,0,,The Chancellor uses him to defend against the Qiang,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:55.35,0:26:58.78,Default,,0,0,0,,so they would naturally withdraw without a fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:59.52,0:27:02.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Meng Huo, the King of the South, is paranoid.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.03,0:27:06.78,Default,,0,0,0,,The Chancellor sends Wei Yan\Nto maneuver with decoys,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.06,0:27:10.42,Default,,0,0,0,,so the Southern troops dare not advance.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:11.82,0:27:13.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Meng Da is a close friend of Li Yan.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:13.85,0:27:16.86,Default,,0,0,0,,The Chancellor used a letter with\NLi Yan's handwriting to persuade him.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:16.86,0:27:18.54,Default,,0,0,0,,How could Meng Da attack?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:18.72,0:27:23.34,Default,,0,0,0,,As for Cao Zhen's force, Zhao Yun has\Nall passes and chokepoints in control.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:23.34,0:27:28.02,Default,,0,0,0,,As the saying goes: "When one man defends\Nthe pass, ten thousand men cannot pass."
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.26,0:27:31.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Zhen had no choice but to withdraw.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:33.62,0:27:36.38,Default,,0,0,0,,With only Eastern Wu remaining\Nout of the five forces,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:36.39,0:27:39.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, do you wish\Nto seek peace with Shu,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:39.36,0:27:41.42,Default,,0,0,0,,or to seek peace with Wei?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.18,0:27:50.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness could not predict the outcome of the five forces, so you stood by.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.56,0:27:54.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Wu is isolated and powerless.\NHow can it defeat Shu?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:56.62,0:27:59.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, after burning\Nseven hundred {\i1}lǐ{\i0} of linked camps,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.94,0:28:03.58,Default,,0,0,0,,we Eastern Wu could also\Nrout the Shu army.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:04.18,0:28:06.34,Default,,0,0,0,,What is there to fear?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:09.90,0:28:12.82,Default,,0,0,0,,They all say that Eastern Wu\Nhas many able men.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.10,0:28:16.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Upon seeing you today, \NI hesitate to say so.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:16.94,0:28:20.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, three kingdoms stand:\None strong, two weak.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:20.33,0:28:24.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Only Wu and Shu joining together \Nto fight Wei could even the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.37,0:28:27.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Otherwise, with one dependent on the other,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:28.15,0:28:30.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Wu would certainly fall after Shu falls.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:32.22,0:28:34.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Such an obvious deduction,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:34.37,0:28:38.54,Default,,0,0,0,,an important minister of state could not have missed it.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:38.54,0:28:40.86,Default,,0,0,0,,If you knew but choose to ignore it,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.02,0:28:43.91,Default,,0,0,0,,is it benefiting your state or harming it?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:46.31,0:28:50.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I am here to seek friendly relations between\NWu and Shu, to clear up misunderstandings,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:50.29,0:28:51.90,Default,,0,0,0,,and to relieve a danger for Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:51.90,0:28:55.61,Default,,0,0,0,,However, that cauldron means\NYour Highness only bears ill will.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.61,0:28:58.55,Default,,0,0,0,,When the realm hears of this, \Nhow could it not attract ridicule?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:58.55,0:29:02.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, I shall die in front of Your Highness\Nto show everyone under Heaven:
Dialogue: 0,0:29:02.70,0:29:04.74,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Do not come to Wu in good faith!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.74,0:29:07.14,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Let this cauldron boil away this diplomat!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:07.51,0:29:08.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Observe!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:13.10,0:29:14.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop him!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:18.10,0:29:21.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, if you wish to cook me,\Nthen why stop me?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:21.33,0:29:22.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Why stop me?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:30.22,0:29:32.66,Default,,0,0,0,,His Highness asks sir to come\Nto the back chamber to talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:45.98,0:29:47.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:48.61,0:29:51.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, our goals are aligned.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:52.21,0:29:55.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I intend to seek peace with your nation,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:55.40,0:29:58.10,Default,,0,0,0,,but I fear that your lord,\Nbeing young and inexperienced,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:58.10,0:30:00.46,Default,,0,0,0,,could not carry the deal through to the end.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:00.70,0:30:02.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Though my master is young,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:02.66,0:30:04.82,Default,,0,0,0,,he is assisted by Chancellor Zhuge.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:05.66,0:30:08.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness is a champion of our times,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:08.34,0:30:11.58,Default,,0,0,0,,and Chancellor Zhuge is a leading figure as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:14.68,0:30:18.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, the land of Shu owns\Nthe dangers of mountains and rivers,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:18.31,0:30:20.67,Default,,0,0,0,,while Wu has the defense of the three rivers.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:20.67,0:30:23.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Should we two states ally with each other,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:23.81,0:30:28.58,Default,,0,0,0,,we could conquer the realm together,\Nor stand in a three-way balance.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:28.58,0:30:31.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, should you send gifts of\Nhomage and submit to Wei,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:31.55,0:30:34.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Wei would order Your Highness to pay homage,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:34.26,0:30:37.34,Default,,0,0,0,,and have your Crown Prince\Nenter Wei as a hostage.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:38.05,0:30:41.70,Default,,0,0,0,,If Your Highness refuses,\NWei would attack,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:42.14,0:30:46.34,Default,,0,0,0,,and our nation would too sail down the river and take your land.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.73,0:30:52.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, I'm afraid the Southlands\Nwould no longer be yours!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:57.34,0:31:02.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Truly, Zhuge Liang is wise in recognizing talent\Nand knows how to employ people.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:03.18,0:31:05.02,Default,,0,0,0,,You, sir, have lived up to expectations.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:05.23,0:31:09.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Come, I shall ally with your land of\NShu to fight against the land of Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:10.30,0:31:11.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:19.06,0:31:21.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Sirs, who would like to be the envoy?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:20.14,0:31:23.26,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(575,455)}Zhāng Wēn\NStyled: Huìshù
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.63,0:31:26.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I would like to enter Shu.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:28.82,0:31:29.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Huishu?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:30.10,0:31:32.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You dare to go and see Zhuge Liang?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:32.11,0:31:34.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you express my sentiment well?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:34.66,0:31:36.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang is human too.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:36.42,0:31:38.90,Default,,0,0,0,,What do I have to fear?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:44.56,0:31:47.93,Default,,0,0,0,,This is our gifted literati of Eastern Wu.\NHis name is Zhang Wen.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:48.15,0:31:50.30,Default,,0,0,0,,He is currently General of the Household.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:51.79,0:31:53.49,Default,,0,0,0,,An honor to meet you at last.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:53.78,0:31:55.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, I dare not.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:55.45,0:32:00.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Let us feast to celebrate Wu and Shu establishing\Nrelations and ceasing hostilities forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:22.34,0:32:23.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, you must not!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:27.05,0:32:27.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:27.94,0:32:28.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Dismissed!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:28.88,0:32:30.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You must not!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:33.30,0:32:34.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:35.86,0:32:37.33,Default,,0,0,0,,This is...?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:38.08,0:32:41.06,Default,,0,0,0,,His name is Qin Mi, a scholar of Yi Province.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:43.66,0:32:45.50,Default,,0,0,0,,You may be a scholar...
Dialogue: 0,0:32:44.62,0:32:52.86,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(300,467)}Qín Mì\NStyled: Zǐchì
Dialogue: 0,0:32:45.63,0:32:48.90,Default,,0,0,0,,But are you, sir, truly well-educated?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:49.71,0:32:53.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Even toddlers in the land of Shu are well-educated,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:53.11,0:32:55.86,Default,,0,0,0,,let alone myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:58.10,0:33:01.06,Default,,0,0,0,,What area of knowledge have you studied, sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:03.62,0:33:07.70,Default,,0,0,0,,From astronomy to geography,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:08.09,0:33:12.70,Default,,0,0,0,,from the Three Religions and Nine Schools to\Nthe Hundred Schools of Thought, everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:12.78,0:33:17.98,Default,,0,0,0,,From the rises and falls to\Nthe classics and scripture, all.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:18.17,0:33:20.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, since you speak with such self-regard,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:20.66,0:33:23.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}please answer my questions about the sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.59,0:33:25.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Does the sky have a head?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:25.29,0:33:26.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}It does!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:27.98,0:33:29.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Where is its head?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:29.91,0:33:31.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}The west.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:32.54,0:33:37.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}As the {\i1}Classic of Poetry{\i0} says:\N"God turned His kind regards to the west."
Dialogue: 0,0:33:32.54,0:33:37.94,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: From Classic of Poetry: Da Ya, Decade of King Wen, Huang Yi. Translation by James Legge.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:38.42,0:33:42.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Inferring from this, the head is to the west.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:42.51,0:33:44.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Does the sky have ears?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.74,0:33:47.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}The sky sits high and listens to those below.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:48.54,0:33:50.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}As the {\i1}Classic of Poetry{\i0} says:
Dialogue: 0,0:33:50.54,0:33:55.78,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,From Classic of Poetry: Xiao Ya, Decade of Tong Gong, Lu Ming. Translation by James Legge.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:50.54,0:33:55.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}"The crane cries in the ninth pool of the marsh,\NAnd her voice is heard in the sky."
Dialogue: 0,0:33:57.15,0:34:00.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}How can one hear without ears?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:01.46,0:34:03.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Does the sky have feet?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:03.92,0:34:05.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}It does!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:05.27,0:34:08.98,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: From Classic of Poetry: Xiao Ya, Decade of Du Ren Shi, Bai Hua. Translation by James Legge.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:05.28,0:34:08.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}As the {\i1}Classic of Poetry{\i0} says:\N"Difficult is the way of Heaven."
Dialogue: 0,0:34:08.98,0:34:12.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}How can one walk the way without feet?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:20.45,0:34:22.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Does the sky have a family name?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:22.22,0:34:23.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}How can it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.58,0:34:24.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:24.50,0:34:25.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}It is Liu!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:25.66,0:34:26.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}How do you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:27.12,0:34:30.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}The Son of Heaven's is of the family Liu.\NTherefore, so is the sky's!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:38.38,0:34:39.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.90,0:34:44.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}The Sun rises from the east!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:44.94,0:34:47.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}The Sun rises from the east, \N but falls to the west!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:48.37,0:34:49.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:35:00.46,0:35:03.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Sir, you are a talented gentleman of Eastern Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:04.61,0:35:09.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Since you posed questions of Heaven,\Nyou surely understand its principles well.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:10.46,0:35:12.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660.674)}There are a few of its principles yet unclear to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:12.99,0:35:16.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660.674)}I would like you, sir, to clarify them.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:16.91,0:35:17.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:35:21.06,0:35:22.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Please speak.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.07,0:35:34.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}In the past, after the division of primeval\Nchaos, {\i1}yin{\i0} and {\i1}yang{\i0} were formed.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:36.06,0:35:39.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}The lighter, finer essence floated upwards to become the sky,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:39.31,0:35:42.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}while the heavier, darker essence condensed as the land.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:44.38,0:35:49.14,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Gonggong(共工): In Chinese mythology, a water deity who lost\Na power struggle with another deity (identity differs by account).
Dialogue: 0,0:35:44.38,0:35:48.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Since the defeat of Gonggong\Nand his collision into Mount Buzhou,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:48.78,0:35:52.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}the pillar of Heaven was broken, the sky tilted down towards the northwest,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:52.32,0:35:55.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}and the land listed to the southeast. So I ask...!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:01.10,0:36:06.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}If the sky, being light and fine, floats upwards,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:07.45,0:36:10.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}then why did it tilt down to the northwest?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:11.41,0:36:15.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Also, what lies beyond the sky?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:16.63,0:36:19.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}{\pos(640,660)}Please tell me, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:20.17,0:36:21.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Ummm...Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:36:33.35,0:36:37.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, Shu is full of geniuses indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:38.31,0:36:41.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I am very illuminated today.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:44.62,0:36:47.42,Default,,0,0,0,,All questions posed during \Nthis banquet were but jests.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:47.94,0:36:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course, the ways of keeping peace in the state
Dialogue: 0,0:36:51.38,0:36:53.22,Default,,0,0,0,,have nothing to do with verbal games.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:55.42,0:36:58.42,Default,,0,0,0,,-Please.\N-Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:58.54,0:37:00.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:33.26,0:37:34.78,Default,,0,0,0,,-Minister Zhang.\N-Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:37.45,0:37:40.30,Default,,0,0,0,,These are gifts from my master.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:40.62,0:37:42.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Please accept them, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:42.18,0:37:43.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Such a generous gift...
Dialogue: 0,0:37:43.54,0:37:44.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:37:51.42,0:37:53.90,Default,,0,0,0,,This is wine from His Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:53.91,0:37:56.86,Default,,0,0,0,,He commanded me to see you off, Minister.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:58.81,0:37:59.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:08.40,0:38:09.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:18.24,0:38:19.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Farewell.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:20.14,0:38:21.70,Default,,0,0,0,,We shall meet again.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:23.70,0:38:25.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Minister Zhang, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:30.86,0:38:32.26,Default,,0,0,0,,We shall meet again.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:34.37,0:38:35.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:36.70,0:38:40.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, Chancellor Zhuge,\Nkind and generous,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:40.87,0:38:43.50,Default,,0,0,0,,would like to make a perpetual\Nalliance with Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:43.50,0:38:46.93,Default,,0,0,0,,He has sent Secretary Deng\Nto return the courtesy.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:46.93,0:38:48.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Greetings, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:52.66,0:38:55.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Wu and Shu's alliance must be due\Nto their designs on our Central Plains.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:55.65,0:38:57.66,Default,,0,0,0,,We shall eliminate them first!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:57.90,0:39:02.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, the land of the Central\NPlains is rich but sparsely populated.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:02.25,0:39:05.02,Default,,0,0,0,,It would be wise to develop the army\Nand agriculture there for ten years.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:05.02,0:39:07.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, with enough food\Nand troops, attack Wu and Shu.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:07.98,0:39:09.62,Default,,0,0,0,,A pedant's thought!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:11.02,0:39:14.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Wu and Shu will attack sooner or later.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:14.51,0:39:15.92,Default,,0,0,0,,How could we wait?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:15.93,0:39:20.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, Eastern Wu is protected by the Yangzi\NRiver, which cannot be crossed without ships.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:20.61,0:39:23.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty must lead the expedition personally.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:23.14,0:39:25.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Select a fleet of large and small\Nships to enter the Huai River.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:25.83,0:39:28.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Capture Shouchun, move towards Guangling,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:28.50,0:39:32.62,Default,,0,0,0,,cross the river, and take Nanxu.\NThis is the optimal stratagem.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:33.89,0:39:34.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Hear my edict:
Dialogue: 0,0:39:35.54,0:39:37.25,Default,,0,0,0,,We appoint Cao Zhen as the vanguard,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:37.25,0:39:41.36,Default,,0,0,0,,and appoint Zhang Liao, Zhang He, Wen Pin,\NXu Huang, and others as commanders.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:41.36,0:39:45.38,Default,,0,0,0,,We shall lead the three hundred thousand\Nmen Ourself against Eastern Wu!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:45.38,0:39:46.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:46.78,0:39:50.32,Default,,0,0,0,,We hereby appoint Sima Yi as "Supervisor of \Nthe Imperial Secretariat," and stay in Xuchang.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:50.32,0:39:53.50,Default,,0,0,0,,All matters of state will be left to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:53.50,0:39:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:58.37,0:40:03.38,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang held off the five armies with ease\Nand reforged the alliance between Wu and Shu.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:03.73,0:40:05.81,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Cao Pi, outraged upon hearing this news,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:05.81,0:40:09.70,Thinking,,0,0,0,,led his armies and navy\Npersonally to attack Eastern Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:10.46,0:40:12.73,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang, upon hearing Eastern Wu's distress,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:12.73,0:40:17.27,Thinking,,0,0,0,,immediately ordered Zhao Yun to lead troops\Nout of Yangping Pass to attack Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:17.98,0:40:20.65,Thinking,,0,0,0,,As Zhao Yun secured one victory after another,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:20.65,0:40:23.58,Thinking,,0,0,0,,an insurrection broke out in the south of Shu-Han.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:23.49,0:40:27.74,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang quickly summoned\NZhao Yun to withdraw in haste,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:27.74,0:40:31.82,Thinking,,0,0,0,,and return to Chengdu in preparation\Nfor an expedition southwards.
Comment: 0,0:11:15.28,0:11:17.53,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: This would require Kebineng's army to travel all the way across Wei.
Comment: 0,0:11:26.78,0:11:28.50,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: "yuè jùn" being an incorrect pronunciation.
Comment: 0,0:21:36.18,0:21:37.98,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Here Lu Xun addresses Sun Quan as the Marquis of Wu, not the Prince of Wu, even though Sun Quan has been made a prince already.

